  "narrative": "No assessments are due. The central evidence is already strong for feature_002=1 (higher composite dependency score), feature_010=1 (higher score), and feature_037=1 (lower, more strongly dependent score), with validation and multiple subgroup persistence. The main unresolved scientific questions are: (1) whether the near-threshold reverse residual feature_003 association in the core-flag-free background is reproducible in assay contexts, and (2) whether any additional rare binary predictors have residual associations outside the three core flags.\n\nI registered six direct feature_003 contrasts in the core-flag-free population, split by approximate halves of the three standardized research signatures feature_038, feature_018, and feature_036. The claimed direction is the same as the prior reverse residual estimate: feature_003=1 associated with a lower outcome_001, i.e. more negative score. If any context estimate exceeds 0.15 units in the signed direction with adequate lower bounds, this would support a context-dependent or stable residual feature_003 signal. If all halves are near null or have upper bounds below the threshold, the original near-threshold estimate is more likely sampling variation or a subthreshold association.\n\nI also registered residual screens for five untested rare binary features (feature_013, feature_016, feature_027, feature_050, feature_063) within the same core-flag-free eligibility. These test whether additional binary predictors carry independent association not masked by the three core flags. The positive claim direction is nominal because these features have no assigned biological role; large opposite-direction effects would be handled as reversed follow-up claims. If threshold-exceeding effects appear, they merit focused validation; if upper bounds are below threshold, the independent-marker screen can be closed as null. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal effects or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 6 explore plan: Core marginals are closed and validated: feature_002=1 higher, feature_010=1 higher, feature_037=1 lower outcome_001. Priority now is residual signal resolution. New batch uses core-free eligibility (feature_002=0, feature_010=0, feature_037=0). It tests feature_003 negative direction by feature_038/018/036 median splits (ge 0 and le 0) and by feature_040 high/low already registered, plus five untested rare binary residual screens. If feature_003 contexts or residual binaries exceed threshold, consider validation or focused refinement. If not, treat residual feature_003 as unresolved near-null and shift to broad categorical/assay interactions already registered. Avoid exact continuous exposure values; use inequalities only."
